---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import PageBanner from "../components/PageBanner.astro";
const updated = "8 August 2026";
---

<PageLayout title="Cookie Policy | Innovative Gloves" description="How Innovative Gloves uses cookies and similar technologies on this website, and how you can manage them.">
  <PageBanner eyebrow="Legal" title="Cookie Policy"
    intro="What cookies are, how this website uses them, and how you can control them." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files that a website stores on your device when you visit. They are widely used to make websites work, to remember your preferences, and to provide information to the site owner. Similar technologies such as local storage work in the same way, and we refer to them all as "cookies" here.</p>

      <h2>2. How we use cookies</h2>
      <p>We keep our use of cookies to a minimum. We use them to make the site function properly and, where enabled, to understand how visitors use the site so we can improve it. We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles or to sell your data.</p>

      <h2>3. Types of cookies we use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strictly necessary.</strong> These are required for the website to work, such as remembering your cookie choices or keeping the site secure. They cannot be switched off through our site.</li>
        <li><strong>Preferences.</strong> These remember choices you make, such as your language, so the site behaves the way you expect.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics and performance.</strong> Where enabled, these help us understand which pages are visited and how the site performs, using aggregated, non-identifying information. If we use a third-party analytics provider, it may set its own cookies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Third-party cookies</h2>
      <p>Some cookies may be set by third parties that provide services to us, for example a website-analytics provider. These providers have their own privacy and cookie policies, which govern how they handle information collected through their cookies.</p>

      <h2>5. Managing cookies</h2>
      <p>You can control and delete cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers let you refuse or remove cookies, and to be notified when a site tries to set one. The exact steps vary by browser, so check your browser's help pages. Please note that blocking some cookies may affect how parts of this website work.</p>

      <h2>6. Do Not Track</h2>
      <p>Some browsers offer a "Do Not Track" setting. Because there is no common industry standard for how sites should respond to it, this website does not currently respond differently to Do Not Track signals.</p>

      <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "last updated" date above.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions about our use of cookies? Email <a href="mailto:sales@innovativeglove.com" class="inline-link">sales@innovativeglove.com</a>. For more on how we handle personal information, see our <a href="/privacy" class="inline-link">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 760px; }
  .legal-updated { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 30px 0 10px; }
  .legal p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .legal ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .legal li { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text); }
  .inline-link { color: var(--green-dark); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
